    "bio": "Rae started tattooing the way most stubborn people do — hand-poking her own ankle in a college apartment, then apprenticing under a traditional shop in Garden City until the machine felt like a pencil. She went private not long after: no walk-ins, no five chairs buzzing at once, just one client and one drawing at a time. Blackwork and single-needle fine line are home base; she takes color projects when the idea genuinely needs it. If your concept isn't a fit, she'll say so and point you to someone in the valley who's better for it.",
